# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Custom-prompt eval for Wan2.1-Fun-V1.1-1.3B-InP — the **i2v anchor route**.
#
# The prompt block above is copied verbatim from
# Wan2.2-TI2V-5B-custom-prompt-eval.sh, so the two model families are read on the
# same narratives.
#
# GEOMETRY (keep equal across arms — long-video metrics are length-sensitive):
# fpc=45, motion window m=5 → stride 40 new frames per chunk, so NUM_CHUNKS=24
# gives 45 + 23*40 = 965 frames. That matches the 5B k3 arms' stride of 40, so a
# fixed chunk count yields the same video length in both families. The base arm's
# --num_frames 965 is the single-pass equivalent of the same 24 chunks.
#
# fpc IS NOT THE SAME ON EVERY ARM, because the trim is not. Each chunk regenerates
# the frames its conditioning already covers and drops them, so the stride is
# fpc - trim, and the trim is a property of the anchor:
#
#   arm                   conditioning              trim  fpc  stride  24 chunks
#   1 base (single pass)  --                          --   --      --  965
#   2 chunk-by-chunk      1 frame via input_image      1   41      40  961
#   3 anchored            m=5 window + ref padding     5   45      40  965
#   4 e2e-ttt             same + LoRA scratchpad       5   45      40  965
#
# So arm 2 runs fpc=41, NOT 45: the stock I2V path hands forward a single frame and
# trims 1, so 45 there would give stride 44 and 1057 frames — 10% longer than every
# arm it is read against. (The 5B script does the same thing for the same reason: 41
# on its plain arm against 53 on its k=3 ones.)
#
# fpc / m / ref_pad_num / resolution come from the meta-training config
# (model_training/configs/Wan2.1-Fun-V1.1-1.3B-InP-e2e-ttt-fomaml.yaml); do not
# change them on the TTT line without changing them on the checkpoint.
#
# Every driver below takes the WHOLE prompt list in one invocation, so the DiT +
# umt5-xxl + VAE + CLIP are read off disk once per arm instead of once per prompt.
# Each prompt still writes to its own
# ./results/custom-prompts-1.3B/<num_chunks>-chunks/<prompt[:30]>/ subdirectory;
# add --skip_existing to resume an interrupted run.
#
# Convention: keep exactly ONE line below uncommented per run.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NUM_CHUNKS=24
OUT_DIR="./results/custom-prompts-1.3B/$NUM_CHUNKS-chunks"
SCRIPT_DIR="/home/hzhao/ttt-imagine-diffsynth/examples/wanvideo/model_inference/custom-prompts"

# phi_0 checkpoint. The run writes at steps 500/1000/1500/2000/2500 plus a final
# step-<N>; point this at the one you mean to sample.
CKPT_DIR="/work/nlp/hzhao/checkpoints/e2e-ttt/Wan2.1-Fun-V1.1-1.3B-InP_e2e_ttt_fomaml_i2v_m5_480p_fpc45_r128_reffirst_antidrift_svi_uvl_fs_rsfps16_len_grouped_3k-20260816-215630"
LORA="$CKPT_DIR/step-375.safetensors"

# ── Arm 1: single-pass base (no chunking). NOTE this checkpoint is image-conditioned,
# so without --input_image it runs on NULL image conditioning — it is "this model with
# nothing given", not a plain T2V base. Frame ladder for other chunk counts: 45 + (N-1)*40.
# python "$SCRIPT_DIR/Wan2.1-Fun-V1.1-1.3B-InP-base-custom.py" --prompt "${PROMPTS[@]}" --negative_prompt "$NEGATIVE_PROMPT" --num_frames 965 --output-dir "$OUT_DIR" --height 480 --width 832

# ── Arm 2: chunk-by-chunk, stock single-frame I2V continuity (motion-unidentifiable anchor).
# fpc=41, not 45 — this arm trims 1 frame, not 5, so 41 is what gives it stride 40. See GEOMETRY.
# python "$SCRIPT_DIR/Wan2.1-Fun-V1.1-1.3B-InP-chunk-by-chunk-custom.py" --prompt "${PROMPTS[@]}" --negative_prompt "$NEGATIVE_PROMPT" --num_chunks "$NUM_CHUNKS" --frames_per_chunk 41 --output-dir "$OUT_DIR" --height 480 --width 832

# ── Arm 3: chunk-by-chunk with the FULL E2E-TTT i2v anchoring, base weights, no LoRA —
# the no-adaptation ablation of the TTT arm below. Keep --num_chunks / --frames_per_chunk /
# --num_motion_frames / --ref_pad_num / resolution in sync with it.
# python "$SCRIPT_DIR/Wan2.1-Fun-V1.1-1.3B-InP-chunk-by-chunk-anchored-custom.py" --prompt "${PROMPTS[@]}" --negative_prompt "$NEGATIVE_PROMPT" --num_chunks "$NUM_CHUNKS" --frames_per_chunk 45 --num_motion_frames 5 --ref_pad_num -1 --output-dir "$OUT_DIR" --height 480 --width 832

# ── Arm 4: E2E-TTT. The inner-loop flags MUST mirror the checkpoint:
# --optimizer adamw (the CLI default is sgd), --inner_lr_init 1e-5, --num_gradient_steps 2,
# --lora_rank 128, --num_motion_frames 5, --ref_pad_num -1.
python "$SCRIPT_DIR/Wan2.1-Fun-V1.1-1.3B-InP-e2e-ttt-custom.py" --prompt "${PROMPTS[@]}" --negative_prompt "$NEGATIVE_PROMPT" --num_chunks "$NUM_CHUNKS" --frames_per_chunk 45 --algorithm "fomaml" --lora "$LORA" --output_name "Wan2.1-Fun-V1.1-1.3B-InP_e2e_ttt_fomaml_i2v_m5_480p_fpc45_r128_reffirst_antidrift_svi_3k.mp4" --output-dir "$OUT_DIR" --num_gradient_steps 2 --optimizer "adamw" --inner_lr_init 1e-5 --lora_rank 128 --num_motion_frames 5 --ref_pad_num -1 --height 480 --width 832
